{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact MCP Apps contract-oracle head 01770f1d8f29680a56fbca40fedd86103d829cd2 on builder/mcp-contract-oracle-20261104, tree 5f932c1c, for request dc800768 under promise 7c23c426 and review request 9daab91a. This approval covers the test-only oracle, the vendored schemas, the owner and fixture changes, the dependency declarations, the workflow filters, the note and the four manifests. It claims no host acceptance, no older-revision conformance for ui/update-model-context and no cause for 64552d40.\n\nScope. Main 333fe65f is an ancestor, and the worktree is clean. Product source and the generated card don't change: the head touches packages/mcp/browser only in bridge.test.ts. The commit-message check passes for all 3 commits. Card run 41791544431 passes at the frozen head c0ab999f. The head adds only the note and two manifests after that commit, so the run covers its card paths.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Independence. I fetched both schemas and licenses from modelcontextprotocol/ext-apps at the pinned commits. All four files match the vendored copies byte for byte. The oracle reads method names and payload definitions only from those schemas' $defs and checks each digest before parsing. It imports no dap type and no fixture handler.\n- The validators are not vacuous. None of the card's outbound definitions uses $ref, so validating a detached $defs entry is sound. In my own probe with the pinned zod 4.4.3, the validators accept the real shapes. They reject an object content, the assistant role, a missing params, a string width, an unknown display mode and an empty initialize params.\n- Revisions. The initial ui/initialize validates against the revision it offers, and later messages validate against the negotiated revision. For 2025-11-21, the oracle admits ui/update-model-context only with an observed -32601 reply to the same id, and records it as a refused extension. The owner asserts that refused extensions appear only in legacy cases.\n- Coverage. verify() now runs the oracle in every existing case that calls it, not only in the twelve new cases. The owner fails unless all seven outbound methods appear.\n- The real caller control. The driver swaps the content array in packages/mcp/browser/main.ts for an object and rebuilds the card. It then asserts the actual stderr: AssertionError, INDEPENDENT MCP CONTRACT McpUiMessageRequest, expected array at params.content. It also checks the failure proof: no chat, no model turn and one -32602 refusal. The restored hashes 235d31f2… and b4a8d6b3… equal main.ts and generated.ts at the head.\n- Strict host. views-host.ts still refuses a non-array content with -32602, and the owner still asserts the exact content array.\n- Dependencies. The lockfile change only declares @modelcontextprotocol/core 2.3.1 and zod 4.4.3 in the MCP workspace, and both nodes resolve at those versions on main 333fe65f.\n\nCompiler and failure honesty. The initial gate at e1899840 reads exit 1, and its 134 originals stay retained. The URL, byte and decoder fixes each keep their own retained run. The fix imports Node's URL and decodes with an explicit TextDecoder and changes no schema, validator or assertion.\n\nThe gate passed. At c0ab999f, gate.exit reads exit 0. All five stages pass: kernel, 134 Node, 56 Counting, 3,614 plain with one skip, and 1,070 Native with two skips. before.json and after.json match, with a clean status and lockfile 5a717d43…, which equals the committed lockfile. The receipt lists no owned process still present.\n\nEvidence. All 130 public files match their sizes and digests and are read-only. All nine SHA256SUMS files match, no unit holds an unlisted file, and the credential scan finds no match. The private inventories match on every file: 773 focused, 928 loader across four units, 2,276 complete-gate with 39 selected, and 12 each for the two Card CI units. All are mode 0400.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The oracle stays in test support and checks wire shapes against the upstream contract. The scripted host stays a separate, stricter witness.\n\nSecurity: no finding. No new resolved package enters, and the vendored files equal upstream.\n\nSimplification: no required change. Three notes for later work:\n\n- The oracle checks shapes, not capability negotiation. In the no-optional cases the host declares no message capability, yet the card still sends ui/message and relies on the -32601 refusal. A later request can decide whether the card should check hostCapabilities first.\n- The oracle validates a detached $defs entry. That works for today's outbound methods. In 2026-01-26, ui/notifications/host-context-changed refers to #/$defs/__schema0, so validating it would need the root schema.\n- The note doesn't name the focused manifest's SHA-256, eac32d88…. The other three are named.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:51fb68d2dd6f467fd8a0cf448fc7b4cf8668346b","binding":"assigned","head":"01770f1d8f29680a56fbca40fedd86103d829cd2","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2a285130569c2302aa05b8529e7aff5fb00dccae\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7c23c426b85b0a7a5df31357b446900ad20bdd62\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2a285130569c2302aa05b8529e7aff5fb00dccae","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}